From 0ad7861aa1028f2f3289b070e357237a10e31e51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noktoborus <noktoborus@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: axp20x: take the power-off before the default handlers
 when system power controller

On 7.3 the watchdog of the BCM2712 (bcm2835_wdt) registers its power-off
handler, a halt of the SoC by the firmware, with SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT when
its node is the system power controller. It probes first; the handler of
the AXP gets -EBUSY, and poweroff leaves the board of the uConsole on.
On 6.12 the watchdog set pm_power_off only when it was empty, and PSCI had
set it.

A PMIC with system-power-controller in its node registers its handler
with SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT + 1: it runs first and powers the whole board
off. Without the property nothing changes.
---
 drivers/mfd/axp20x.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c b/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
index 50df66de24e..f46c2b1e184 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
@@ -1458,8 +1458,17 @@ int axp20x_device_probe(struct axp20x_dev *axp20x)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A PMIC that is the system power controller powers the whole board
+	 * off: its handler runs before the others of the default priority.
+	 * On the BCM2712 the watchdog registers a halt of the SoC there
+	 * first, and this one would get -EBUSY.
+	 */
 	if (axp20x->variant != AXP288_ID)
-		devm_register_power_off_handler(axp20x->dev, axp20x_power_off, axp20x);
+		devm_register_sys_off_handler(axp20x->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF,
+					      of_device_is_system_power_controller(axp20x->dev->of_node) ?
+					      SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT + 1 : SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT,
+					      axp20x_power_off, axp20x);
 
 	dev_info(axp20x->dev, "AXP20X driver loaded\n");
 
